{
  "case_id": "2022-22-138",
  "document_hash": "e617c1b6e0761a5928ba09e55046773046208e9a0a2619ce287e213ffee51abc",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-22-138",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e617c1b6e0761a5928ba09e55046773046208e9a0a2619ce287e213ffee51abc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e617c1b6e076-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nJOHN P. ELWOOD, ESQUIRE, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nPHILIP J. WEISER, Attorney General, Denver, Colorado; on behalf of the Respondent.\nERIC J. FEIGIN, Deputy Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-22-138",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e617c1b6e0761a5928ba09e55046773046208e9a0a2619ce287e213ffee51abc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e617c1b6e076-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Mr. Elwood, I don't quite understand why you would cite Black when Black did have an intent requirement. The question was whether or not the presumption of cross-burning in a field overcame that -- that intent requirement or demonstrated that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "John P. Elwood (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2022-22-138",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e617c1b6e0761a5928ba09e55046773046208e9a0a2619ce287e213ffee51abc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e617c1b6e076-0000-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Criminalizing misunderstanding is especially dangerous in an age when so much communication occurs on social media, which brings together strangers in an environment that removes much of the context that gives words meaning. And it chills expression by imposing prison time on speakers who do not tailor their views to suit their audience."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE BARRETT",
      "case_id": "2022-22-138",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e617c1b6e0761a5928ba09e55046773046208e9a0a2619ce287e213ffee51abc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e617c1b6e076-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "BUT LET'S IMAGINE -- I -- LET'S IMAGINE THIS EXAMPLE: LET'S SAY THAT, YOU KNOW, A TEENAGER IN A HIGH SCHOOL SAYS SOMETHING LIKE, YOU KNOW, I'M GOING TO SHOOT THIS PLACE DOWN, AND IT'S DEVOID OF ALL CONTEXT."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. ELWOOD",
      "case_id": "2022-22-138",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e617c1b6e0761a5928ba09e55046773046208e9a0a2619ce287e213ffee51abc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e617c1b6e076-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "BUT ONE EXAMPLE IS GLENN SCHUMACHER IN ILLINOIS, WHO IS A 58-YEAR-OLD MARRIED MAN WHO, ON THE COMMENTS PAGE OF A LOCAL NEWSPAPER, THE ELMHURST PATCH, RESPONDED TO AN ARTICLE ABOUT, YOU KNOW, LITTERING AND CROWDS AND SO FORTH AT AN ANNUAL EVENT BY SAYING PERHAPS A FEW PLACED -- WELL -- PRESSURE COOKER POTS. AND THE VERY NEXT COMMENTER SAID, YOU KNOW, WE ALL APPRECIATE SOME CLEVERNESS AND HUMOR, BUT THAT'S PRETTY CRASS. SO, CLEARLY, THE FIRST PERSON WHO SAW IT IMMEDIATELY KNEW IT WAS A JOKE. HE WAS ARRESTED AT 2 A.M. THE NEXT DAY AND HELD FOR SIX WEEKS ON A BOND THAT HE COULD NOT AFFORD UNTIL HE PLEADED GUILTY TO ESSENTIALLY DISORDERLY CONDUCT."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-22-138",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e617c1b6e0761a5928ba09e55046773046208e9a0a2619ce287e213ffee51abc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e617c1b6e076-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm trying to understand whether you're saying that in every other category of unprotected speech we require some subjective intent, with perhaps the exception of fighting words. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-22-138",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e617c1b6e0761a5928ba09e55046773046208e9a0a2619ce287e213ffee51abc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e617c1b6e076-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Are you saying that you have to always prove somebody intended to commit the act, or do you have to just say that they knew they were going to put someone else in fear?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent (Philip J. Weiser)",
      "case_id": "2022-22-138",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e617c1b6e0761a5928ba09e55046773046208e9a0a2619ce287e213ffee51abc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e617c1b6e076-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "True threats have always been prosecuted without protection by the First Amendment. Petitioner now seeks to impose a specific intent element onto this inquiry that's required neither by history nor precedent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-22-138",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e617c1b6e0761a5928ba09e55046773046208e9a0a2619ce287e213ffee51abc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e617c1b6e076-0002-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF PHILIP J. WEISER ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent (Philip J. Weiser)",
      "case_id": "2022-22-138",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e617c1b6e0761a5928ba09e55046773046208e9a0a2619ce287e213ffee51abc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e617c1b6e076-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Imposing a specific intent requirement would thwart the goals of the First Amendment, enabling more harm and leading to less valuable discourse."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-22-138",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e617c1b6e0761a5928ba09e55046773046208e9a0a2619ce287e213ffee51abc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e617c1b6e076-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The statute talks about the manner of the communication. So do you say that the statute --you interpret the statute to mean that a person cannot be convicted based on the manner of making communications, the content of which is not in themselves threatening?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-22-138",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e617c1b6e0761a5928ba09e55046773046208e9a0a2619ce287e213ffee51abc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e617c1b6e076-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why isn't the defendant's intentions part of the context? How could it not be part of the context?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2022-22-138",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e617c1b6e0761a5928ba09e55046773046208e9a0a2619ce287e213ffee51abc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e617c1b6e076-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Are you saying --I want to follow up on Justice Gorsuch's questions to you about stalking. He was asking you about physically following people, and -- and you said Colorado has such a statute -- can I finish, Chief?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Eric J. Feigin",
      "case_id": "2022-22-138",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e617c1b6e0761a5928ba09e55046773046208e9a0a2619ce287e213ffee51abc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e617c1b6e076-0003-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 85,
        "start": 85
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Just to make clear what's on the table, the question presented as framed by Petitioner invokes only a specific intent and knowledge question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Feigin)",
      "case_id": "2022-22-138",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e617c1b6e0761a5928ba09e55046773046208e9a0a2619ce287e213ffee51abc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e617c1b6e076-0004-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FEIGIN: Well, to be clear, Your Honor, our frontline position is that there shouldn't be a recklessness standard at all."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-22-138",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e617c1b6e0761a5928ba09e55046773046208e9a0a2619ce287e213ffee51abc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e617c1b6e076-0004-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: But you're saying that the historical record supports, clearly supports, that no mens rea is required?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-22-138",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e617c1b6e0761a5928ba09e55046773046208e9a0a2619ce287e213ffee51abc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e617c1b6e076-0004-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 90,
        "start": 90
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Hold on."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Feigin)",
      "case_id": "2022-22-138",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e617c1b6e0761a5928ba09e55046773046208e9a0a2619ce287e213ffee51abc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e617c1b6e076-0004-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 94,
        "start": 94
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Number one, you know, just -- number one is that it enables very devious defendants -- again, when Elonis did get in on the -- did get on the stand, he said, I didn't care what other people thought."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "John P. Elwood",
      "case_id": "2022-22-138",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e617c1b6e0761a5928ba09e55046773046208e9a0a2619ce287e213ffee51abc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e617c1b6e076-0005-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 108,
        "start": 108
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ELWOOD: Just a few points. The burden is on the proponents of restrictions on speech to justify it both as a legal matter, as a constitutional matter, and as a -- as the practicalities of bringing it. I think the burden is on them to show that it would cause a problem."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-22-138",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e617c1b6e0761a5928ba09e55046773046208e9a0a2619ce287e213ffee51abc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e617c1b6e076-0005-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 110,
        "start": 110
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And Justice Scalia, writing for the Court in United States versus Williams, said, in a speech case, child pornography, courts and juries every day pass upon knowledge, belief, and intent having before them no more than evidence of the defendant's words and conduct from which an ordinary human experience mental condition may be inferred."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-22-138",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e617c1b6e0761a5928ba09e55046773046208e9a0a2619ce287e213ffee51abc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e617c1b6e076-0005-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 112,
        "start": 112
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 12:06 p.m. the case was submitted.)"
    },
    {
